Find the missing limits in the repeated integral below

[MATH: \displaystyle \iiint \limits_{R} f(x,y,z) \: \textrm{d}V
=
\int_{\ast}^{\ast}
\int_{\ast}^{\ast}
\int_{\ast}^{\ast}
f(x,y,z) \: \mathrm{d}x \: \mathrm{d}z \: \mathrm{d}y]

where [MATH: R] is the type II region defined as

[MATH: R=\left\{ (x,y,z) \: : \: 1 \leq y \leq 4, \: -y^2 \leq z \leq \sqrt{y}, \: -2 \leq x \leq ye^{z+2} \right\}.]
